3:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Four Reasons Forms Don't Get Filled"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-6","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"1. The Page Hasn't Earned The Ask Yet"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If your form appears before there's any proof - testimonials, outcomes, specifics, credibility signals - you're asking for trust you haven't built. The visitor's internal calculation is: \"I don't know if this works, I don't know if this person delivers, and they're asking me for my information.\" That's a no. Proof belongs above the form. Always. One specific result or a named outcome immediately before the form field lifts completion rates measurably because it answers the doubt that was stalling the click."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"2. The Form Asks Too Much"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Every field you add to a form costs approximately 10% of completions. That's not a metaphor - it's the consistent pattern across form optimisation data. A form with name, email, phone, company, company size, and \"tell us about your situation\" is a five-decision obstacle, not a form. For most B2B lead gen, the minimum viable form is name and email. If you need a phone number, ask for it after the initial conversion - in a follow-up email or on a thank-you page. You can earn additional information once there's already a relationship."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"3. Friction Language On The Button"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["\"Submit\" is the single worst word on a conversion button. It communicates nothing about what happens next and subtly frames the action as something being done to the visitor. Button copy should describe the outcome the visitor receives: ",["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"\"Get my free audit\""}]," instead of \"Submit.\" ",["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"\"Send my leak report\""}]," instead of \"Send.\" The copy should answer: what do I get when I click this? If the answer isn't in the button, the button is working against you."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-2 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"4. No Privacy Reassurance Near The Field"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["Visitors who hesitate at a form are often running a quick threat model: \"If I give them my email, am I going to get spammed?\" A single line directly below the email field - ",["$","span",null,{"className":"italic text-fg","children":"\"No spam. One email with your results.\""}]," - reduces that hesitation significantly. It doesn't need to be a long privacy policy link. It needs to be a plain-language promise positioned exactly where the doubt arises: right below the input field, not buried in a footer."]}]]}]]}]]}]
4:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"How To Diagnose Where The Real Leak Is"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Before you touch the form, get the diagnostic data:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-3 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Heatmaps:"}]," Where are visitors dropping off before the form? If scroll depth shows most visitors leave at the 30% mark and your form is at 70%, you have an above-the-fold trust problem - not a form problem."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Session recordings:"}]," Watch 10 recordings of visitors who didn't convert. Look for rage-clicks (repeated frustrated clicking), back-navigation immediately after scroll, and hover-then-abandon on the CTA button. Each of these signals a different break in the chain."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-1 h-2 w-2 flex-shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","span",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Form scroll depth:"}]," Are visitors reaching the form at all? If fewer than 30% of sessions scroll to the form, the problem isn't the form - it's everything above it. If 70% reach the form but only 2% fill it, the form and its surrounding context is the issue."]}]]}]]}]]}]
5:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"The Form Fix Checklist"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Once you've confirmed the form zone itself is the leak (visitors reach it but don't fill it), work through this in order:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 flex h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-accent text-accent text-xs font-bold","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Reduce to minimum viable fields."}]," Name + email for most B2B. Add phone only if your follow-up is exclusively by phone and you can justify the ask."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 flex h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-accent text-accent text-xs font-bold","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Rewrite the submit button to name the outcome."}]," \"Get my free audit,\" \"Send my leak report,\" \"Start the diagnosis\" - specific, outcome-oriented, first person."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 flex h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-accent text-accent text-xs font-bold","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Add a single line of proof directly above the form."}]," One specific outcome from a real user. Not a logo wall - a specific result that makes the decision feel safer."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 flex h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-accent text-accent text-xs font-bold","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Remove competing navigation."}]," Header nav links and footer menus near the form give the visitor an exit option at the moment of peak intent. Strip them from the conversion zone."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-border p-4","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-0.5 flex h-5 w-5 flex-shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full border-2 border-accent text-accent text-xs font-bold","children":"✓"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg-muted","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Add a no-spam line directly below the email field."}]," Short, plain, positioned precisely at the point of doubt. \"No spam. Your results, once.\" is enough."]}]]}]]}]]}]
